Addons and plugins cannot expose internal API as far as I know.
In any case, using separate plugin to expose single getter for property is ugly.
I just can't think of any good reason why one-way property for shapes must be set-only in PhysicsServer2D.

### Proposed improvement

'body_is_shape_set_as_one_way_collision' method must be added to PhysicsServer2D and in inherited classes.
```C++
bool GodotPhysicsServer2D::body_is_shape_set_as_one_way_collision(RID p_body, int p_shape_idx) const {
	GodotBody2D *body = body_owner.get_or_null(p_body);
	ERR_FAIL_NULL_V(body, false);
	ERR_FAIL_INDEX_V(p_shape_idx, body->get_shape_count(), false);

	return body->is_shape_set_as_one_way_collision(p_shape_idx);
}
```
This method must be exposed to engine users as well.
After this, one-way shape detection with Area2D becomes very trivial:
```GDScript
func _is_shape_one_way(body_rid: RID, body_shape_index: int) -> bool:
	return PhysicsServer2D.body_is_shape_set_as_one_way_collision(body_rid, body_shape_index)
```
I have successfully implemented this method in my custom Godot build.
I'm ready to write pull request.

